        <div><a name="sec-LimitOfOpenWater" id="sec-LimitOfOpenWater"></a><h2>4.6<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Limit of Open Water</h2>

<div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;"><a name="_23a3d6a1-ec87-9bd1-2101-2025d08c5af7" id="_23a3d6a1-ec87-9bd1-2101-2025d08c5af7"></a><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1a9c68a1-71e1-b818-954a-33f8261897de" id="_1a9c68a1-71e1-b818-954a-33f8261897de"></a><u><b>IHO Definition</b> :</u> The demarcation at any given time between sea ice and freely navigable water, in which sea ice is present in concentrations less than 1/10.</p>
