        <div><a name="sec-IceKeelBummock" id="sec-IceKeelBummock"></a><h2>4.20<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Ice Keel/Bummock</h2>

<div align="center" class="table_container"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;"><a name="_54c81065-d001-e78e-5557-6514218cd8bf" id="_54c81065-d001-e78e-5557-6514218cd8bf"></a><tbody><tr><td valign="top" align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2ea5a7f3-530e-fadb-2492-b1974ab9142a" id="_2ea5a7f3-530e-fadb-2492-b1974ab9142a"></a><u><b>IHO Definition</b> :</u> From a submariner&#x2019;s point of view, a Keel is a downward projecting ridge on the underside of the ice canopy&#x2009;&#x2014;&#x2009;the counterpart of a Ridge. A Bummock is the counterpart of a hummock on the underside of the ice canopy.</p>
</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;page-break-after:avoid;"><p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2257148f-d40e-fb38-7e6e-2cf95c79a5f8" id="_2257148f-d40e-fb38-7e6e-2cf95c79a5f8"></a><u><b>S-411 Geo Feature:</b></u> Ice Keel/Bummock</p>
